3. No monetization

You may not monetize the Software or any Modified Version, directly or
indirectly. In particular, you may not:

(a) sell, rent, lease, sublicense for payment, or otherwise charge money or
other consideration for copies, licenses, downloads, distribution, access,
or use of the Software or a Modified Version;

(b) offer the Software or a Modified Version as a paid hosted service,
subscription, managed service, or feature of a paid product or service;

(c) include the Software or a Modified Version in a bundle or product sold
for money or other consideration, even if the Software is described as free;

(d) earn advertising, affiliate, sponsorship, donation, crowdfunding, or
similar revenue specifically tied to developing, distributing, providing
access to, or promoting the Software or a Modified Version; or

(e) charge third parties for installation, hosting, customization, maintenance,
support, consulting, or development of the Software or a Modified Version.

These restrictions apply to every Modified Version, including versions with
substantial new functionality, and to monetization through an intermediary.
You may not remove or evade these restrictions by changing the name, packaging,
license notice, or distribution method, or by adding new functionality.

4. Commercial workplaces and independent work products

You may use the Software or a Modified Version internally in a business,
employment, or professional practice, including to create, edit, and read
documents for paid work. Employees may be paid for internal deployment,
maintenance, and modification for their employer's own use. Such internal use
is not monetization under section 3.

Documents and other independent work products created or edited with the
Software are not governed by this license solely because the Software was
used to create or edit them. You may sell those independent work products or
services based on them, provided you do not distribute, provide access to,
or otherwise monetize the Software or a Modified Version as part of them.

